`./gradlew test --tests com.nereusstream.delay.adapter.BoundedDestinationPublishAdapterTest --tests com.nereusstream.delay.ownership.WorkerPhysicalPublishExecutorTest --tests com.nereusstream.delay.scheduler.OpenTelemetryMetricExporterTest`

Result: `BUILD SUCCESSFUL`. `BoundedDestinationPublishAdapterTest`: 20 tests, 0 skipped/failures/errors; `WorkerPhysicalPublishExecutorTest`: 9 tests, 0 skipped/failures/errors; `OpenTelemetryMetricExporterTest`: 1 test, 0 skipped/failures/errors. `./gradlew checkstyleTest` passed. `./gradlew checkDocumentation` passed. `git diff --check` and `jq empty docs/ndip/NDIP-3/progress.json` passed.

`BoundedDestinationPublishAdapter` starts its monotonic timer after the final bounded preflight allows the request and immediately before invoking the destination delegate. The sample ends when the delegate-returned `CompletionStage<DestinationPublishResult>` completes. It includes synchronous adapter preparation/validation and result-stage mapping; it excludes physical admission/adapter-executor wait, final preflight work, and the subsequent Worker Outcome handoff. Completion means the adapter result became observable; it does not independently certify an authoritative business result. Preflight rejection emits no send-stage sample. Missing or explicitly unobserved stages, or failed completion callback registration, increment `TARGET_PHYSICAL_PUBLISH_STAGE_UNAVAILABLE`. Both events have fixed cardinality and no Target/Shard attributes, and are offered to the optional caller-owned bounded async metrics queue. `WorkerPhysicalPublishExecutor` and `BoundedDestinationPublishAdapter` expose optional composition overloads; existing constructors keep metrics disabled.

The adapter regression verifies preflight rejection does not call the delegate, an observed asynchronous result yields one duration event, and a null delegate stage yields unavailable. The OTel SDK `InMemoryMetricReader` verifies both new instrument values, units, and empty attributes. This is local adapter-stage instrumentation evidence. No production `WorkerPhysicalPublishExecutor` construction/provider configuration caller was found, so this does not prove runtime enablement or real Broker latency.

`./gradlew checkstyleMain` failed only on the existing untouched line-length findings: `PersistentLaneScheduler.java:1327` and `TargetWorkerHostRuntime.java:377` (123 characters each). No new source violation was reported.

E4 remains `IN_PROGRESS / PENDING_CENTRAL_VALIDATION`; device I/O/WAL, remaining read paths, production provider/config, certification mode/generation/coverage, restart/gap coverage, and central validation remain open.

